        <tr id="comment-body-7415392"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Editing previous assessment based on additional information provided by the <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddcb525f313007008badb" class="user-hover" rel="617ddcb525f313007008badb" data-account-id="617ddcb525f313007008badb" accountid="617ddcb525f313007008badb" rel="noreferrer">Shawna Maitia</a>  and <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Aa202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" class="user-hover" rel="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" data-account-id="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" accountid="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" rel="noreferrer">Hina Khan</a> </p>

<p>This use case is <b>Medium Risk</b>. This is an advisory rating and does not approve/deny the use case. Per question support available: <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ISRM/pages/1917255764/AI+Risk+Assessment+Process+Support+Guide" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ISRM/pages/1917255764/AI+Risk+Assessment+Process+Support+Guide</a> </p>

<p><b>Overall Risk Profile:</b></p>

<p>The rating is driven by use of generative AI in agent-facing member service workflows, third-party Pega capabilities, regulated health plan operations, and potential member impact through guidance, searches, summaries, and recommendations. Risk is reduced by the requestor’s clarification that Knowledge and Coach do not access, store, or save PHI or PII, Knowledge retrieves procedural SMP articles, Coach operates on configured business rules and masked case context, prompts are not used for model training, and BSC controls data exposure, knowledge sources, user access, and partner access.</p>

<p><b>Recommended Mitigation Actions:</b></p>

<p>To reduce the risk, document the confirmed PHI and PII exclusion design, identify the exact data fields and knowledge sources available to Knowledge and Coach, maintain masking and role-based access controls, confirm prompt and output retention settings, complete contract and governance approvals, validate security and resilience controls, and establish monitoring for accuracy, relevance, compliance adherence, access violations, and inappropriate data exposure.</p>

<p><span class="nobr"><a href="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/3081408" title="GAI-663_AIRiskAssessment_Edited.xlsx attached to GAI-663" data-attachment-type="file" data-attachment-name="GAI-663_AIRiskAssessment_Edited.xlsx" data-media-services-type="file" data-media-services-id="413116e9-e24e-4a22-8b18-b8f29c6e7c15" rel="noreferrer">GAI-663_AIRiskAssessment_Edited.xlsx<sup><img class="rendericon" src="/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif" height="7" width="7" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/></sup></a></span> </p>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7418614"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:efc9ce40-9a67-4d81-be61-30d8958f6525"
                id="word_commented_712020:efc9ce40-9a67-4d81-be61-30d8958f6525"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aefc9ce40-9a67-4d81-be61-30d8958f6525">
                    Saipradeep Bomma
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">31/Jul/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7418614"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddcb525f313007008badb" class="user-hover" rel="617ddcb525f313007008badb" data-account-id="617ddcb525f313007008badb" accountid="617ddcb525f313007008badb" rel="noreferrer">Shawna Maitia</a>  thanks for the clarification. To make sure the assessment is documented correctly, can you please confirm the following or attach supporting documentation?</p>

<ul>
	<li>Does Knowledge Buddy access, store, save, transmit, or retain any PHI or PII?</li>
	<li>Does Knowledge Buddy only retrieve SMP knowledge articles?</li>
	<li>Can you confirm SMP knowledge articles contain only agent desktop procedures and do not store PHI/PII?</li>
	<li>Does Coach access, store, save, transmit, or retain any PHI or PII?</li>
	<li>Does Coach only use business rules and summarize interaction history for the user?</li>
	<li>Where is the interaction history stored?</li>
	<li>Can you confirm the data remains stored in Pega Customer Service and that this storage has been in place since 2019?</li>
	<li>Do the AI capabilities only help execute searches and make recommendations?</li>
	<li>Are prompts, outputs, summaries, logs, telemetry, or interaction history stored by Knowledge Buddy, Coach, Pega, or any partner outside the existing Pega Customer Service environment?</li>
	<li>Are any prompts, outputs, summaries, logs, telemetry, or interaction history used for model training, tuning, or improvement?</li>
</ul>


<p>Once this is documented, I can use it to update the assessment as appropriate.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7418669"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="617ddcb525f313007008badb"
                id="word_commented_617ddcb525f313007008badb"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddcb525f313007008badb">
                    Shawna Maitia
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">31/Jul/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7418669"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <ul>
	<li>Does Knowledge Buddy access, store, save, transmit, or retain any PHI or PII? No</li>
	<li>Does Knowledge Buddy only retrieve SMP knowledge articles? It can retrieve knowledge from other sources as we determine necessary.  For customer service their knowledge base is SMP Knowledge Articles.</li>
	<li>Can you confirm SMP knowledge articles contain only agent desktop procedures and do not store PHI/PII? Yes.</li>
	<li>Does Coach access, store, save, transmit, or retain any PHI or PII? No</li>
	<li>Does Coach only use business rules and summarize interaction history for the user? Yes, and it can make recommendations based on rules.</li>
	<li>Where is the interaction history stored? Interaction history is stored in a couple places. Pega Customer Service and also other various sources such as Facets which Pega Customer Service pulls in via API service calls.  Coach and Knowledge is not pulling in PHI or PII data from these API service calls.</li>
	<li>Can you confirm the data remains stored in Pega Customer Service and that this storage has been in place since 2019? Yes</li>
	<li>Do the AI capabilities only help execute searches and make recommendations? Yes</li>
	<li>Are prompts, outputs, summaries, logs, telemetry, or interaction history stored by Knowledge Buddy, Coach, Pega, or any partner outside the existing Pega Customer Service environment? No</li>
	<li>Are any prompts, outputs, summaries, logs, telemetry, or interaction history used for model training, tuning, or improvement? No, customer prompts submitted to GenAI Coach are not used for model training, tuning, or product improvement. Coach receives its prompt instruction from within Infinity Studio through Pega.  Additionally, the Coach can be contained to only use information contained within Pega or your content/data behind the firewall and not be exposed to the internet</li>
</ul>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7418782"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:efc9ce40-9a67-4d81-be61-30d8958f6525"
                id="word_commented_712020:efc9ce40-9a67-4d81-be61-30d8958f6525"
