                    Saipradeep Bomma
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">31/Jul/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7418782"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Thanks<a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddcb525f313007008badb" class="user-hover" rel="617ddcb525f313007008badb" data-account-id="617ddcb525f313007008badb" accountid="617ddcb525f313007008badb" rel="noreferrer">Shawna Maitia</a>, that clarification helps.<br/>
Can you please clarify whether Coach receives, processes, or uses any of the following:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Live call audio</li>
	<li>Call transcripts</li>
	<li>Call recordings</li>
	<li>Interaction notes</li>
	<li>Interaction summaries</li>
	<li>Prompts used for model training, tuning, or improvement</li>
</ol>


<p>If yes to any of the above, please confirm whether the data contains any PHI, PII, member-specific information, claims, benefits, or other identifiable member data. If the data is anonymized, de-identified, or limited to procedural/business-rule content only, please confirm that as well.</p>

<p>Also, please describe what controls prevent PHI/PII from being provided to Coach, and whether Pega or any partner has rights to use prompts or related data beyond BSC’s controlled purpose.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7419089"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="617ddcb525f313007008badb"
                id="word_commented_617ddcb525f313007008badb"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddcb525f313007008badb">
                    Shawna Maitia
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">31/Jul/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7419089"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Can you please clarify whether Coach receives, processes, or uses any of the following:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Live call audio - No</li>
	<li>Call transcripts - No</li>
	<li>Call recordings - No</li>
	<li>Interaction notes - Potentially, if interaction notes are stored within the host application and intentionally provided as case context to Coach. GenAI Coach is designed to provide guidance based on application and case data.</li>
	<li>Interaction summaries - Not out of the box.  If BSC so chooses, you could add these as a knowledge source or tool for Coach later on if it is a requirement for the Coach to use this info. </li>
	<li>Prompts used for model training, tuning, or improvement - No, customer prompts submitted to GenAI Coach are not used for model training, tuning, or product improvement. Coach receives its prompt instruction from within Infinity Studio through Pega.  Additionally, the Coach can be contained to only use information contained within Pega or your content/data behind the firewall and not be exposed to the internet.</li>
</ol>


<p>If yes to any of the above, please confirm whether the data contains any PHI, PII, member-specific information, claims, benefits, or other identifiable member data. If the data is anonymized, de-identified, or limited to procedural/business-rule content only, please confirm that as well. - This data can be masked (configured in the data portion of Infinity Studio) and will only be available to Coach in its masked form.</p>

<p>Also, please describe what controls prevent PHI/PII from being provided to Coach, and whether Pega or any partner has rights to use prompts or related data beyond BSC’s controlled purpose. - You maintain access to which case data is made available to the Coach, which knowledge sources it can see and which user populations can access the coaching capabilities and what is exposed to end users.</p>

<p>In summary, GenAI Coach is a case guidance and workflow coaching capability. Based on the information reviewed, it is <b>not designed to process live call audio, call recordings, or transcription streams</b>. Coach operates on application and case context configured by the BSC and therefore only accesses member, claims, benefits, PHI, or PII information if such data is intentionally made available through the hosting application. This is a great source for additional trust and security information <a href="https://urldefense.com/v3/__http://www.pega.com/trust__;!!NvsU1QEulwjNNrcOZ0amcNU!gxsqif-a1AMcMtCtz7Zq-DG3Z6X4vVXIp7HSxGG48xP0CgYv1l3esZIVFtOAuvNA7dEHWpTz6d8HCwRGSXiT8JOlAgsl$" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><ins>http://www.pega.com/trust</ins></a>.</p>

<p> The only way Pega and Partner access would be granted to view your data would be based on roles BSC provides to those respective individuals to the respective applications.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7441464"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:abf20bfc-ead7-40ab-96e9-8412d17fa0bc"
                id="word_commented_712020:abf20bfc-ead7-40ab-96e9-8412d17fa0bc"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aabf20bfc-ead7-40ab-96e9-8412d17fa0bc">
                    Delia Johnson
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">06/Aug/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7441464"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Does <b>Pega Knowledge (Content Buddy)</b> and <b>Coach AI</b> provide any decisions to members on calls?  Does it provide medical/clinical information to members on calls? If yes - how is the determination made to provide specific replies that are medical or clinical in nature?</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7441573"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
